    "long_instructions": "## Lighting Designer\r\n\r\nMake the spotlight use a different color each time the program runs.\r\n\r\n1. Review the code and ask AI Tutor how `set_fill_color()` and `Color()` work.\r\n2. Create variables for red, green, and blue.\r\n3. Use `randint()` to store a random value in each variable. Each color value can be from 0 to 255. \r\n4. Update the spotlight color command to use your variables.\r\n5. Run the program several times and observe what changes.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "from theater import *\nfrom random import randint\n\n# Background\nset_fill_color(\"black\")\ndraw_rectangle(0, 0, 400, 400)\n\n# Sparkling light beam\nset_fill_color(Color(255, 0, 255))\ndraw_shape([200, 155, 90, 330, 310, 330], True)\n\n\n# Disco ball string\nset_stroke_color(\"white\")\nset_stroke_width(2)\ndraw_line(200, 0, 200, 45)\n\n# Disco ball\nset_fill_color(\"silver\")\ndraw_ellipse(145, 45, 110, 110)\n\n# Disco ball mirror tiles\nset_stroke_color(\"white\")\nset_stroke_width(1)\n\n# Vertical tile lines\ndraw_line(170, 55, 170, 146)\ndraw_line(200, 45, 200, 146)\ndraw_line(230, 55, 230, 146)\n\n# Horizontal tile lines\ndraw_line(150, 80, 250, 80)\ndraw_line(145, 110, 255, 110)\ndraw_line(159, 140, 239, 140)\n\n# Dance floor\nset_fill_color(\"purple\")\ndraw_rectangle(0, 330, 400, 70)\n\n# Sparkles\nset_text_color(\"white\")\nset_text_height(50)\ndraw_text(\"*\", 95, 95)\ndraw_text(\"*\", 280, 85)\ndraw_text(\"*\", 90, 205)\ndraw_text(\"*\", 300, 220)\n\n\n# Music notes\nset_text_color(\"aqua\")\nset_text_height(28)\ndraw_text(\"♪\", 55, 210)\ndraw_text(\"♫\", 330, 190)\n\n# Title\nset_text_color(\"white\")\nset_text_height(28)\ndraw_text(\"Disco Lights\", 115, 385)\n\n# Sound\nplay_note_and_pause(72, 0.25)\nplay_note_and_pause(79, 0.25)\n\nplay()",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
